    "body": "fix on issue/1904-continuous-4axis-walkthrough · PR #2346 · pinned by `continuous_4axis_part` (5 tests, `crates/app/tests/continuous_4axis_part.rs`) and `FirstContinuousFourAxisProgram` (13 tests, `site/tests/test_first_continuous_4axis_part.py`) · merges when reviewed, after PR #2342 (stacked on it)\n\nThe continuous half: the guide page \"Your first continuous 4-axis program\", the demo project `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` with its program and model, and three drawn pictures.\n\nTwo limits found, both filed:\n- #2343: Rotary Parallel finishes the model's end faces down to the axis. On a bar held in a chuck that is a cut through the bar, and no setting stops it. So the page ends with an air cut (no bar in the chuck) and tells the reader not to cut.\n- #2344: Rotary Offset takes two laps of A for each level that cuts, so the PathPilot post refuses it on the microARC 4 file (A travel -360..360).\n\nNot done: the program has no PathPilot Hub run yet (\"Done means\" asks for a run to M30). The page's section \"Prove it in the PathPilot simulator\" lists five things to check; please record the run here. Wrapping a drawing round a cylinder is not implemented, so the page has no wrapped engraving. If this is not enough to close the issue, the PR's `Fixes` should become `Refs`.\n\nAlso filed #2345: three site tests fail on main, unrelated to this work.\n",
